>> title: Cuernos
>> category: Breads
>> tags: bread, mexican, sweet, enriched, oven
>> counters: Panadería
>> aka: cuerno, cuernos, cuernito, cuernitos, mexican crescent, pan cuerno, sweet crescent roll
>> pairs-with: pan-dulce-dough, conchas
>> servings: 12
>> time: 2 hr
>> step.1: roll a circle and cut 12 triangles
>> step.2: roll up, curve, proof 90 min
>> step.3: wash and bake at 350°F 16 min

Roll @masa para pan dulce{800%g}(three-quarters of a batch, chilled) into a 14-inch circle on a bench dusted with @all-purpose flour{2%Tbs}(16 g), then cut it into 12 wedges like a pie.

Roll @&(~1)wedges{} up from the wide base to the point, lay them point-down on trays greased with @vegetable shortening{1%Tbs}(14 g), bend the ends in to a crescent, and ~proof{90%min} until puffed and light.

Brush @&(~1)proofed crescents{} with @beaten egg{1%large}(50 g) and bake at 350°F for ~bake{16%min}, until they are the colour of a brown egg.
